# ============================================================================
# CogniWeb Agent - Direct dependencies
# ============================================================================
# VERSION POLICY: every dependency carries an UPPER BOUND (< next.major)
# so a clean install can never silently pull an untested major release
# (e.g. openai jumped 1.x -> 3.x with renamed exception classes while this
# code was written against 1.x semantics). The exact tested set is frozen
# in lock.txt; raise a bound only after running the test
# suite against the new major.
#
# NOTE ON HASH-PINNING (TZ fix #6, docs vs code drift): an earlier version
# of this header promised `pip-compile --generate-hashes`, but neither
# base.txt (curated bounded ranges) nor lock.txt (plain `pip freeze`
# snapshot) carries --hash= entries today. Supply-chain protection is
# therefore provided by exact version pins + `pip-audit` in CI, NOT by
# per-file hashes. If you enable hash-pinning later, regenerate with:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes requirements/base.in -o requirements/base.txt
# and update this comment to match reality.
# ============================================================================

